---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="Arnav Attri" current="about">
  <div class="intro">
    <img src="/1.jpeg" alt="Arnav Attri" width="960" height="1280" class="portrait" loading="eager" decoding="async" />
    <div>
      <h1>Arnav Attri</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Teaching Fellow, <a href="https://plaksha.edu.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Plaksha University</a></p>

      <p class="lead">
        I teach CS and AI courses at Plaksha University and conduct independent research in natural language processing with frontier LLMs, across both closed- and open-source models.
      </p>
      <p class="lead muted" style="margin-bottom:0">
        Before joining Plaksha in August 2025, I completed my M.Tech. <a href="https://www.cse.iitb.ac.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">(CSE-TA) at IIT Bombay</a>, working at the <a href="https://www.cfilt.iitb.ac.in/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">CFILT Lab</a> with Flipkart's research team under the guidance of <a href="https://www.cse.iitb.ac.in/~pb/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Prof. Pushpak Bhattacharyya</a>. Most of my papers are written with <a href="https://openreview.net/profile?id=~Anuj_Attri1" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Anuj Attri</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>News</h2>
  <ul class="rows">
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Nov 2026</span>
      <span>Reviewing for ICLR 2027, The Web Conference 2027, and ACL ARR Oct 2026.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Aug 2026</span>
      <span><a href="/research/#punjabi-safety">Same Intent, Different Script</a> published in Findings of EMNLP 2026.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Jul 2026</span>
      <span><a href="/research/#cognition-affect">Bridging Cognition and Affect</a> published in Findings of ACL 2026.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Dec 2025</span>
      <span>Co-designed the programming challenges for all 5 days of the modular course <em>Reasoning with LLMs</em> at Plaksha (taught by Dr. Niket Tandon, Microsoft Research India).</span>
    </li>
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Oct 2025</span>
      <span><a href="/research/#m-os">LLMs as Architects and Critics</a> published in Findings of IJCNLP-AACL 2025.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Aug 2025</span>
      <span><a href="/research/#eot-x">Why We Feel What We Feel</a> published in Findings of EMNLP 2025; joined Plaksha University as a Teaching Fellow.</span>
    </li>
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Jun 2025</span>
      <span>Graduated from IIT Bombay with an M.Tech in Computer Science and Engineering.</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Reviewer</h2>
  <ul class="rows">
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Current</span>
      <span>ICLR 2027 · The Web Conference 2027 (Long Papers) · ACL ARR Oct 2026</span>
    </li>
    <li class="news-row">
      <span class="news-when">Past</span>
      <span>NeurIPS 2026 · ACL ARR Aug 2026</span>
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Background</h2>
  <ul class="rows">
    <li>
      <div class="row-head">
        <strong>M.Tech, Computer Science and Engineering (TA) · IIT Bombay</strong>
        <span class="muted small tnum">2023 – 2025 · GPA 8.85/10</span>
      </div>
      <p class="small muted" style="margin:6px 0 0">
        Advisor: <a href="https://www.cse.iitb.ac.in/~pb/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Prof. Pushpak Bhattacharyya</a> (<a href="https://www.cse.iitb.ac.in/memorial" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">in loving memory</a>). Scored <strong>10/10</strong> in Master's Thesis Project Part 1 (MTP1), Part 2 (MTP2), and Research &amp; Development Project (R&amp;D 1), all conducted at CFILT Lab with Flipkart's research team. Also administered the lab's Nvidia A40 GPU servers and was nominated among 7 students for IIT Bombay's Dr. Shankar Dayal Sharma Gold Medal.
      </p>
    </li>
    <li>
      <div class="row-head">
        <strong>UGC-NET Qualified</strong>
        <span class="muted small tnum">2017</span>
      </div>
      <div class="small muted">Eligible for Assistant Professor in Computer Science and Engineering.</div>
    </li>
  </ul>
</Layout>
